  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ROY T. ENGLERT, JR., ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nTHOMAS G. HUNGAR, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nCARTER G. PHILLIPS, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But may I not ask, Isn't it true that each of the parties here, over a long period of time, was a purchaser? I mean, the -- Reeder was a purchaser, was he not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas G. Hungar",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUNGAR: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The fundamental question in this case is whether a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But how can you say -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "point is, the price discrimination does not occur when there is any competition. And, therefore, the requirements of the Act are not satisfied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Two -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What evidence was there of competition here? How -- did you bring forward instances where they both bid for sale of special trucks to a single repurchaser?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have any instance where you made an offer to a buyer assuming that you'd get the kind of a break that Volvo gives to other dealers -- all right? -- you made that offer, and the buyer says, \"Yes, I'll take it at that price\" -- and then you go to Volvo, and they won't give you that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oh, sure. We had thousands of those examples."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the evidence is absolutely overwhelming, because you have a situation where, in 1995, we are next-to-none dealer for Volvo. In 1995, we're selling 66 cars, we're making $165,000. Volvo implements its \"Volvo Vision,\" the purpose of which is to drive my client out of this dealership. It engages in systematic discrimination, both with respect to unquestionable purchases on both sides and, candidly, more broadly than that. And the effect of that, at the end of the day, is that our sales go from 65 to 34 to 18 to 8. Our gross profits dropped to $26,327."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Supposing you did have a contract, such as Justice Scalia suggests, in which the manufacturer agreed that, at any given point of time, you will get just as favorable a concession as any other Volvo dealer could get at the same time. If there were such a contract in place, would the evidence show that it was breached?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It seems to me that's a jury question. And the jury found in our favor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roy T. Englert",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The heart of the theory of this case came up in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Phillips' response was, \"That's today, Your Honor. But our future ability to compete is impaired.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "customer, New Hi-Way, which was 82 percent of its business, was bought by a Memphis company."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Let me ask you, if you have a minute left, is your central point that there was no proof of damages or no proof of injury to competition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-905",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11f1bb15a9cc24cd0878ebd5f3aa087000a9a65cd60f5bf5fc08214e26537e7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11f1bb15a9cc-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
